.TH CBMAP_CONSTRUCT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cbmap_construct \- type-safe BST map construction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cbstmap.h>

cbmap_construct(hm_name, key_type, val_type);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-safe macro for creating a BST map with default settings.
Automatically determines the key type (signed/unsigned integer,
floating-point, string, or other) and creates type marker variables for
compile-time type checking.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm_name   Name of the BST map variable to create
key_type  Type of keys
val_type  Type of values
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Terminates program on allocation failure
Uses default memory management and comparison
For a struct key_type, this falls back to a raw memcmp ordering; see
cbmap_create_full(3) for the default-comparison rules and how to
supply a custom_comparison_proc instead (the cbmap_construct_cc
macro is the type-safe equivalent for a struct key_type)
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cbmap_construct(map, int, char*);
cbmap_insert(map, 42, "hello");
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_create (3),
.BR cbmap_create_full (3)
